# Roadmap — {{project.name}}

> Project roadmap. Each MVP is a **fully deliverable piece of work** — independently deployable, testable, and demonstrably valuable. **MVPs build on each other** — MVP 1.1 assumes MVP 1.0 is complete and archived.

## MVP Lifecycle

> **VEP 2.0 authority boundary — this rule governs the entire document.**
> OpenSpec is optional draft input only until the adapter materializes and installed VEP validates
> `.visu/work/<change-id>/contract.yaml`. From that transition onward, A1 is the sole editable
> semantic and implementation-plan authority. `proposal.md` and `tasks.md` are deterministic,
> hash/version-bound read-only projections. Roadmaps, trackers, agents, commands, and skills are
> non-authoritative guidance. Any instruction below to create, edit, tick, merge, or reverse-sync
> those views after A1 exists is superseded. Amend A1 through the adapter, revalidate, and regenerate.
> Direct projection edits, stale bindings, mixed versions, and cross-change reuse must stop without mutation.


```
openspec/changes/mvp-X.Y/          ← Active MVP
  progress-tracker.md              ← Tracks all REQs / BUGs / ENHs for this MVP
  REQ-X.Y-001/proposal.md          ← Individual requirement proposals
  REQ-X.Y-001/tasks.md
  BUG-X.Y-001/proposal.md

                ↓ All Done + Tests Pass

openspec/archive/mvp-X.Y/          ← Completed MVP (historical)
  progress-tracker.md
  REQ-X.Y-001/...
```

**Archiving rule:** When every row in `openspec/changes/mvp-X.Y/progress-tracker.md` is `Done` and the full test suite passes, move the entire `openspec/changes/mvp-X.Y/` folder to `openspec/archive/mvp-X.Y/` and update the MVP status in this file to `Completed`. The next MVP folder becomes the active working directory.

